ch integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) there exists a configuration of \\(n\\) distinct lines fulfilling the covering condition and containing exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.  \nConversely, because we are allowed only \\(n\\) lines, no configuration can contain more than \\(n\\) sunny lines. Therefore the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;k\\in\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}\\; } .\n\\] ∎\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
